# Docker only reads .dockerignore from the root of the build context —
# since docker/backend.Dockerfile and docker/frontend.Dockerfile are both
# built with the PROJECT ROOT as context (see their header comments), this
# is the file that actually takes effect. backend/.dockerignore and
# frontend/.dockerignore exist too (for anyone building from within those
# subdirectories directly), but Docker does NOT read them when building
# from the root the way docker-compose.yml does here.

**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/coverage
**/uploads
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
.git
.gitignore
README.md
docs
